app orb-shell-renderers-spec [
  version: "1.0.0",
  description: "Targets ios and android (orb shell-renderers ios|android [--out <dir>] [--registry <file>] [--lists <file>]): the per-pattern renderer files under renderers/<pack>/renderers/<tier>/ are hand-owned and committed, and the command generates only what the registry drives. It reads the patterns registry (default orbital-rust/crates/orbital-shell-typescript/core/dist/patterns/patterns-registry.json), the shared pattern-lists.json of the iOS pack (deferred, Rust-drawn canvas and fixed-size lists, per-tier family comments) and the pack data files stub.tpl and registry.tpl. It writes CorePatternRegistry.swift or .kt (registry.tpl with one entry per non-deferred, non-canvas pattern, native when its file exists and holds no wrench-emoji placeholder and the fallback renderer otherwise, then the canvas aliases and the Rust canvas hosts), the pack package.json (the orbRenderer block with the core version and the sorted coverage list), a stub file from stub.tpl for each pattern with no file, and removes orphan files (a deferred, canvas or unregistered pattern) unless --out is given, in which case everything is written under <dir> mirroring the pack and nothing is removed. It also generates AlmadarBreakpoints, AlmadarSizes and VerificationIds (.swift or .kt) from the pack's native-tokens.json and the breakpoints.tpl, sizes.tpl and verification-ids.tpl templates, and checks every existing per-pattern file against the body gates (chrome tokens, raw color and bare numeric literals outside a theme accessor, atom-owned primitives in non-atom tiers, Swift local declarations, Android subcompose roots without almadarFlexFill, declared required and event props referenced), each violation printed as `  - [gate] pattern: detail` after `error: N gate violation(s):`, status 500. Targets dioxus and tui (orb shell-renderers dioxus|tui [--out <dir>] [--registry <file>] [--mapping <file>] [--lists <file>]): the per-pattern .rs files under renderers/<pack>/src/components/<domain>/<tier>/ are hand-owned; for each domain (dioxus: core and game, tui: core) the command writes the four tier mod.rs files, the domain mod.rs, register.rs (register.tpl of the pack, one use and one register line per renderer in tier then collation order, an alias that is the Pascal case module name plus Renderer, prefixed by the tier when taken, Rust keywords as r#), and src/components/mod.rs; a registry pattern of the domain (component-mapping importPath under /components/<domain>/, avl too for core) with no file gets stub.tpl (tui only) and a placeholder file or a leftover wrench-emoji file answers `error: N placeholder renderer(s), implement a real renderer for each:` with one indented path per line, status 500; a file with the generated dioxus header whose pattern left the registry is removed (with --out it is only counted). Success answers `<target>: <domain> N renderers (M stub(s)); ... (K orphan(s) pruned)`. A pack left with a placeholder answers status 500 (exit 1) naming the patterns; otherwise `<target>: N native, M stub(s) written, K orphan(s) pruned` (found with --out), status 200. Target icon-map: Design contract for `orb shell-renderers <target> [--table <file>] [--members <file>] [--out <dir>]`, the generator of the native shells' renderer files (port of tools/almadar-pattern-sync's ios-renderers, android-renderers, icon-map, native-theme, tui and dioxus renderer commands and core-py; one target per generator, landing in order of size). It reads language data from the working directory and writes each shell's generated files under its renderers/<name>/ pack. Target icon-map: reads the icon table (default packages/almadar-ui/lib/iconNativeMap.json, an object `{fallback: {sfSymbol, materialSymbol}, map: {<lucide name>: {sfSymbol, materialSymbol}}}`; --table names another file) and the list of Icons.Filled member names the Android classpath carries (default orbital-rust/crates/orbital-shell-android/renderers/compose/material-icons-filled-members.json, --members names another). Every materialSymbol, the fallback included, is converted to its member and must be in that list: any that is not stops the command before it writes, with `error: N materialSymbol value(s) have no Icons.Filled.* member: <symbol>, <symbol>` (status 500, exit 1). Otherwise it writes IconMap.swift (default orbital-rust/crates/orbital-shell-ios/renderers/swiftui/renderers/) and IconMap.kt (default orbital-rust/crates/orbital-shell-android/renderers/compose/renderers/), or both into <dir> with --out. IconMap.swift is the header line, `import Foundation`, `enum IconMap` holding `static let table: [String: String]` with one line per icon holding the quoted name, a colon and the quoted sfSymbol, and a comma, in code-unit order of the name, `static let fallback` and `resolve`; IconMap.kt is the header line, the Compose imports, `object IconMap` holding `table` (name to Material Symbols name), `fallback`, `resolve`, `vectors` (name to Icons.Filled.<Member>, the member being the symbol split on underscores, each segment capitalised and joined: arrow_back is ArrowBack), `fallbackVector` and `resolveVector`; both end with a newline and quote their strings as JSON does. The answer is `icon-map: N icons, 2 files` (status 200, exit 0). An unknown target, a missing target, a positional word, an unknown or valueless flag, or an unreadable or malformed table answers the usage `usage: orb shell-renderers icon-map [--table <file>] [--members <file>] [--out <dir>]` or `error: cannot read <file>` (status 400 exit 2, and status 500 exit 1)."
]

orbital OrbShellRenderersSpec {
  expects trait OrbShellRenderers {
    state ready
    state reading
    state writing
    emits {
      SHELL_RENDERERS_ANSWERED { status : number!  body : string! }
    }
  }
  expects page "/orb-shell-renderers" -> OrbShellRenderers
}
